# Aristo Dual-Atlas Coordinate System

A Lean 4 project implementing the **Dual-Atlas coordinate functor** over the
prime-power structure of the Monster sporadic simple group `𝕄`. It pairs a small
set of *proven* number-theoretic foundations with two reflection-based coordinate
atlases (a *primal* atlas and its *dual*) and a unified dispatcher, all exposed as
custom Lean elaboration commands.

The whole library builds with `lake build` and contains **no `sorry`**; every
theorem depends only on the standard Lean/Mathlib axioms.

---

## Architecture overview

The system is organised as three layers, each in its own module under
`RequestProject/`:

```
RequestProject/
  Holograms.lean    -- Layer 1: proven mathematical foundations
  AristoTask.lean   -- Layer 2: primal coordinate atlas + #stratify
  DualAtlas.lean     -- Layer 3: dual atlas, dual functor, #dualstratify, #atlas
  Main.lean          -- option/environment scaffold
```

Dependency order is strict and acyclic:

```
Holograms  ──▶  AristoTask  ──▶  DualAtlas
```

