## Layer 1 — `Holograms.lean` (mathematical foundations)

This module records the proven facts the coordinate atlases rest on. The central
object is the order of the Monster group,

```
|𝕄| = 2^46 · 3^20 · 5^9 · 7^6 · 11^2 · 13^3 · 17 · 19 · 23 · 29 · 31 · 41 · 47 · 59 · 71 .
```

| Declaration | Statement |
|-------------|-----------|
| `monsterOrder` | the order `|𝕄|`, as the prime factorisation above. |
| `monster_divisor_count` | `monsterOrder.divisors.card = 424488960`. |
| `monster_threeadic_depth` | every divisor `d ∣ |𝕄|` satisfies `v₃(d) ≤ 20`. |
| `divisors_partition_mod` | for any modulus `m > 0`, the divisors partition by residue mod `m` (the prime-signature partition specialised to `5, 7, 11, 13`). |
| `dualizePair` | the exponent–base swap `(p, e) ↦ (e, p)` (i.e. `p^e ↦ e^p`). |
| `dualizePair_involutive` | `dualizePair` is an involution. |
| `dualizePair_bijective` | hence a bijection of `ℕ × ℕ`. |

The divisor count `424488960` factors as `47·21·10·7·3·4·2^9`, matching the
exponent-plus-one product over the prime factorisation; `monster_divisor_count`
proves this equality.

