## Layer 2 — `AristoTask.lean` (primal atlas)

The primal atlas maps each Lean declaration into *Monster-divisor space* using the
reflected hash of its value.

* `AristoCoordinate { size, cell, depth }` — the primal coordinate.
  * `size` — index into the `424488960`-element divisor space (`h % 424488960`).
    The literal is exactly `Holograms.monsterOrder.divisors.card`; it is used
    directly so the projection stays efficiently computable.
  * `cell` — harmonic cell from the prime-signature partition, via `cellCode`
    (priority `13 > 11 > 7 > 5 > default`).
  * `depth` — semantic recursion depth (`h % 21`), bounded by the 3-adic depth.
* `primalCoord` — the projection `Nat → AristoCoordinate`.
* `primalCoord_depth_le` — `(primalCoord h).depth ≤ 20`, consistent with the
  3-adic depth bound.
* `#stratify f` — reflection command printing the primal coordinate of `f`.

