## Layer 4 — Introspection & the animated SVG comic book

The newest layer lets the source code *see itself* and draw itself into the
atlas.  It is split across three modules.

### `RequestProject/SVG.lean` — native SVG
A small, total SVG abstract syntax tree (`Svg.elem` / `Svg.text` / `Svg.raw`)
with convenience builders (`rect`, `circle`, `line`, `polygon`, `group`) and a
pretty-printer `svgToString` / `render`.  SVG is just another term Lean emits.

### `RequestProject/Introspect.lean` — the projection layer
* `IntrospectivePanel {name, primal, dual, x, y, z, style}` — the abstract
  comic panel for one declaration.
* `mkPanel` / `projectPanel` — reflect a declaration (via `e.hash.toNat`) and
  fuse its primal + dual coordinates into a 3-axis atlas position:
  `x = dual.cog`, `y = primal.depth + 3·dual.triad`, `z = styleOfHarm dual.harm`.
* `#introspect f` — project a single declaration.
* `#atlasmap` — project **every** project declaration and print the sorted map.

### `RequestProject/IntrospectSVG.lean` — the SVG + animation layer
Projects the entire source code into one self-contained **animated 2D/3D SVG
comic book**:

* **Panel I (2D)** — the atlas: cognitive axis (`cog`, 46×2) horizontally,
  semantic axis (`triad`, 20×3) vertically.  One marker per declaration,
  colour-coded by harmonic class and shaped by cognitive-layer band
  (rect / hexagon / octagon / circle / star).
* **Panel II (3D)** — the same atlas in isometric projection with a harmonic
  `z`-lift and a gentle auto-rotation.
* **Chapters 1–3** — one comic page per module (`Holograms`, `AristoTask`,
  `DualAtlas`) with halftone backgrounds and a chip + name for every decl.
* **Animation** — native SMIL (`<animate>` / `<animateTransform>`): staggered
  entrances plus per-harmonic motion (recursion drift, hemisphere oscillation,
  heptad 7-cycle, Muse pulse).

Commands:

```lean
#svgatlas              -- build the comic and report its size
#writecomic "path"     -- build the comic and write the SVG file to `path`
```

The committed artifact `atlas_comic.svg` (with a static PNG preview
