### `RequestProject/Cosmos.lean` — the whole-universe modular + functional view

The atlas layers above project the *project's own* declarations.  This module
zooms all the way out and ingests **every declaration in scope** — the entire
**Lean compiler** (`Lean.*`), the **Lean core / standard library**
(`Init.*`, `Std.*`, `Batteries.*`), and the **whole of Mathlib** (`Mathlib.*`) —
parses the `uses` relation between them straight from Lean's live `Environment`
(the same `getUsedConstants` relation the kernel sees), and renders two
complementary pictures into one self-contained animated SVG:

* a **modular view** — the universe grouped into *ecosystems*
  (Mathlib / Lean compiler / Init core / Std / Batteries / Other), each annotated
  with how many **modules** (source files) and **declarations** it contributes,
  plus a bar-chart breakdown of the dominant **subsystems** inside Mathlib
  (Algebra, CategoryTheory, Analysis, Topology, …) and inside the Lean compiler
  (Meta, Elab, Compiler, …);
* a **functional view** — the aggregated dependency graph: a directed weighted
  graph whose edge `A → B` carries the number of times a declaration in
  ecosystem `A` references one in ecosystem `B` (edge width ∝ the magnitude of
  the weight; hover for exact counts).

At the time of writing the scan covers **707,165 declarations across 9,981
modules** (Mathlib 504,719 / Lean compiler 82,176 / Init 57,532 / Std 44,170 /
Batteries 9,602 / Other).

```
